    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. one thing that worries me though is the lateral movement risk. even with Yubikeys, if a bad actor gets into a workstation through some other way, they might still be able to exploit session tokens or bypass things. what are the biggest \"hidden\" threats we should be looking out for during this transition that aren't just physical loss of the key?",
